      "content": "This sounds like a situation that requires a careful, methodical approach, not just a quick sweep. You'll need to treat this as a potential security breach until proven otherwise, even if the culprit is just a very organized infestation. I suggest you first increase the surveillance coverage in that specific corner, perhaps by temporarily mounting a higher-resolution, night-vision camera. If the footage is still too murky, consider setting up motion-activated cameras with better zoom capabilities near the electrical conduits. If you suspect unauthorized human access, you should also review keycard logs for the basement area during the times these piles appear.",
      "source": "target",
